// A recipe, written from md-docs/recipes/check-a-deploy.md by scripts/docsite/recipes.py;
// edit the recipe, not this file.
page RecipeCheckADeploy(path: "/recipes/check-a-deploy", title: "Check a deploy — Recipes", description: "Check a WebFluent site after each deploy: deep links that reload, text in the HTML, the response headers, link previews and the sitemap.") {
    RecipeShell("Check a deploy", summary: "This recipe is the list to go through after each deploy, on any host: the mistakes it catches pass every check on your own machine.  You need the deployed site's address.  - Open a deep link directly and reload it. A 404 means the host does not fall back to `index.html` (a single-page build), or `base_path` is wrong. - View a page's source. In a static build, the page's text is in the HTML. - Check the response headers in the browser's network panel. - Run a link-preview debugger on a page, and submit `sitemap.xml` to the search engines' consoles.", outputs: ["website", "app"], since: "", recipes: RECIPE_INDEX, sections: [Anchor(id: "how-it-works", label: "How it works")], related: [RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Build a Docker image", to: "/recipes/docker-image"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Deploy to Cloudflare Pages", to: "/recipes/deploy-to-cloudflare-pages"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Deploy to GitHub Pages", to: "/recipes/deploy-to-github-pages")], source: "md-docs/recipes/check-a-deploy.md", how: true, hasVariations: false) {
        Markdown("- A deep link loaded directly is the one request the host answers without the router: the home page can work while every other address is a 404.\n- A static build pre-renders every page, so its text should be in the HTML the host sends ([Static sites and SPAs](/about/static-or-single-page)).\n- The headers show whether the host sends what `build/_headers` holds ([Set cache and security headers](/recipes/cache-and-security-headers)).\n- A link preview and the sitemap use the absolute addresses `meta.site_url` names ([Describe pages to search engines and link previews](/recipes/search-and-link-previews)).\n\nBefore the next deploy, `wf verify` loads every page of the build in headless Chrome and catches a script error, a failed request or a blank page before it ships ([Install wf on a build machine](/recipes/install-wf-in-ci)).")

    }
}
